        "description": "<h4 style='font-weight:400; margin:0.375rem 0px 0.75rem; font-size:1.414rem; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif;'>Description</h4><div style='padding-bottom:0.375rem; max-width:100%; display:inherit; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; box-sizing:border-box; padding:0px; color:rgb(5, 5, 5); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif;'><font size='3' style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='font-family:inherit; box-sizing:border-box; color:var(--dark-800);'>﻿</span><span style='font-family:Calibri; box-sizing:border-box; color:black;'>New Hampshire law (RSA 485:17-a) requires all schools and licensed child care programs to test for lead in drinking water at outlets where water is available for consumption by children. Three rounds of testing are required. This interactive map displays data provided to the NH Get the Lead Out of Drinking Water Program for the various rounds of testing. Generally, sample dates are from 2016-2022. The second and third rounds of testing are currently underway, and the map and dashboard are periodically updated with new data. If no results are found for your school or child care, most likely they have not yet collected samples; contact your school or child care for more information. For more information about testing requirements, </span><a href='https://www.des.nh.gov/water/drinking-water/lead/schools-and-child-care-programs' style='color:rgb(0, 97, 155); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>click here</a><span style='font-family:Calibri; box-sizing:border-box; color:black;'>. NHDES is not responsible for the use or interpretation of this information by third parties. Not for legal use.</span></font></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; box-sizing:border-box; padding:0px; color:rgb(5, 5, 5); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13px; text-align:center;'><span style='font-family:inherit;'><br /></span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; box-sizing:border-box; padding:0px; color:rgb(5, 5, 5); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13px; text-align:center;'><em>This project was funded by USEPA’s Water Infrastructure Improvements for the Nation (WIIN) Act, Lead Testing in School and Child Care Program Drinking Water Grant</em></p></div>",
        "licenseInfo": "Not for legal use.",
